<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet>
    <title>Quiz 5 - MTH 305 - Regan</title>

    <p>
        This quiz covers optimization of mathematical models and a retake on
        sensitivity of mathematical models.
        Read all <term>DIRECTIONS</term> carefully.
        Good luck!
    </p>

    <exercise workspace="5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                A gardener wants to construct 4 garden areas by first building a
                fence around a rectangular region, then subdividing the region
                into 4 smaller rectangles by placing 3 fences parallel to 1 side
                of the rectangle. What dimensions of the region minimizes the amount of fencing if
                the total area of the region is 300 square feet?
                Make sure to show all work and verify that your solution is, in
                fact, a minimum.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                Suppose <m>k</m> is a constant that captures the intrinsic
                strength of a square wooden beam relative to its width (
                <m>w</m> ).
                Given a circular log of 14 inches in diameter, the maximum
                strength for a beam with width <m>w</m> is given by:
                <md>
                    k = \frac{196}{3w^2}
                </md>
            </p>
        </introduction>

        <task workspace="0.5in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Determine the sensitivity function <m>S(k,w)</m> that
                    captures the sensitivity of <m>k</m> to changes in the
                    constant <m>w</m>.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task workspace="0.5in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    What is the sensitivity when <m>w = 13</m> and
                    <m>k = 0.39</m>?
                    Interpret the meaning of your calculation in the context of
                    the scenario.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task workspace="0.5in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    What conclusions can you make about how confident we can be
                    in the output of this model?
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
    </exercise>
</worksheet>